        "runId": "ada-en-work-20261110-mw9trx1d-qy2ds2",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      },
      "text": "Mangroves, swamps and old plantations"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a8704e80dc128a8",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "6b48e541447e0cdf54ac884be5e090ae3662a8339d4f0973283e7234a847623b",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-20261110-mw9trx1d-qy2ds2",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      },
      "text": "Today combines history and nature. You will head to Warappa Creek and pass through mangroves. Along the old plantations, remnants of sugar production survive as the jungle gradually reclaims the land.\n\nYou will visit the former Bakkie plantation and a small private museum that displays objects found on the plantation connected with the lives of enslaved people. After the tour, return to your hotel.\n\nMeals: breakfast and lunch."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_label:91818fadec8b377e",
